// M8c exit scenario (1987): a long defence where ammunition decides. Two Blue M1A1 platoons that
// fought through the night hold the village crossroads with a quarter of their rounds (10 a tank)
// against three Red tank companies attacking one after another. That does not last three attacks: the supply trucks (tailgate), the supply point in the rear
// (service station) and the recovery vehicle keep the defence going. Play as Blue; the Blue AI
// plan (with its resupply and recovery doctrine) is used only when the side is not
// player-controlled (headless runs, tests).
(
    id: "m8c-long-defence",
    name: "LONG DEFENCE",
    date: (1987, 6, 15),
    start_time_s: 19800, // 05:30
    map: (id: "demo", recipe: "rolling-farmland", seed: 42, size_m: 8000.0),
    seed: 5,
    briefing: "SITUATION: A RED TANK BATTALION (KURGAN-A) ATTACKS FROM THE NORTH-EAST BY COMPANIES, ONE AFTER ANOTHER, FROM FIRST LIGHT.\n\nMISSION: 1ST AND 2ND PLATOONS (BULWARK A1) HOLD THE VILLAGE CROSSROADS FOR 75 MINUTES. RED WINS BY HOLDING THE VILLAGE UNCONTESTED FOR 2 MINUTES. A SIDE THAT LOSES 70 % OF ITS TANKS LOSES.\n\nNOTES: THE PLATOONS FOUGHT THROUGH THE NIGHT: EACH TANK HAS 10 OF ITS 40 MAIN-GUN ROUNDS LEFT, NOT ENOUGH FOR THREE ATTACKS. SUP (AMMUNITION AND FUEL TRUCKS) CAN RESUPPLY A PLATOON IN ITS POSITION (R, TAILGATE); SP 1 IN THE REAR SERVES A PLATOON THAT DRIVES BACK TO IT. R (RECOVERY VEHICLE) TOWS IMMOBILISED TANKS TO THE UMCP FOR REPAIR (O). RESUPPLY IN THE LULLS BETWEEN ATTACKS, ONE PLATOON AT A TIME.",
    objectives: [(name: "VILLAGE", centre: (4500.0, 4300.0), radius_m: 350.0)],
    victory: (time_limit_s: 4500.0, objective: "VILLAGE", attacker: 1, destroyed_fraction: 0.7),
